// THE FLEET LEDGER: what each player used from the fleet and what they gave it
// (src/relay/handlers/fleet_ledger.rs, src/relay/storage/fleet_ledger.rs). Read by
// the relay at startup, disk first, the copy built into the exe only when this file
// is missing or does not parse.
//
// The operator decided on 2026-10-04 (question 12 of
// docs/design/ship-homes-and-logistics.md), verbatim: "For the sake of simplicity
// during early development we'll say the fleet has unlimited of everything and just
// track what they player uses and contributes. That way they can be in the red or
// black so they can gauge what they're actually using/contributing."
//
// So the relay keeps, per player key, one line for each thing they used from the
// fleet and each thing they gave it: what, how many, what it was worth then, and
// when (the shared world's game day, and the real day; at the default 72x clock a
// game day is 20 real minutes). The balance is everything given minus everything
// used, in credits (CR): in the black when it is above 0, in the red when it is
// below. A player sees only their own ledger; an admin sees the totals once enough
// players have one. Erasing an account deletes its ledger.
//
// WHAT THE LEDGER TAKES ON TRUST (said plainly, the review of 2026-10-04): the
// server holds no inventories yet (increment 8 of the design), so it takes the
// game's word that a gift was in the backpack, and the game's word for its home's
// power. An unaltered game can still give the same thing twice in one way: with
// "Start every session from the default home" on (the default during development)
// each session starts with the starter kit again, and giving the kit each session
// counts each time. Gifts made in Creative mode are recorded but never counted.
//
//   kinds       one row per kind of line. The relay records exactly these ids (a test
//               checks each one it records is here):
//                 "meal"            a meal a player takes from the ship's food stores
//                                   (the take_meal action, src/relay/handlers/ship_stores.rs);
//                 "item"            items a player gives the fleet at one of its stores;
//                 "item_creative"   items given while the giver's game was in Creative
//                                   mode, which makes things from nothing: recorded so
//                                   the player sees the gift, worth 0 so it never moves
//                                   the balance (the review of 2026-10-04, finding 5);
//                 "power_drawn"     electricity the ship's reactor supplied their home
//                                   (src/systems/ship_power.rs meters it; the game reports
//                                   it while the player is in the shared world);
//                 "power_returned"  surplus electricity their home sent back to the ship.
//               Each row says:
//                 direction  Used or Contributed (which side of the balance);
//                 label      the words the ledger shows;
//                 unit       what `how many` counts ("" for an item: its name is shown);
//                 price      what one unit is worth, in CR:
//                              OfGood("id")  the base_value of that trade good in
//                                            data/trade_goods.ron;
//                              OfItem        the base_value of the item the line is about
//                                            (an item with no trade good there has no price,
//                                            and the fleet does not take it: the give is
//                                            refused and nothing leaves the backpack);
//                              Fixed(n)      n CR per unit;
//                 per_day    true for a flow that never stops (power): one line per real
//                            day, added to as the day goes, instead of one per report.
//                 max_lines_per_day
//                            the most lines of this kind one player may write in one
//                            real day (None: no cap). Gives are capped at 500: a give
//                            every three minutes for a whole day and night is 480, more
//                            than anyone hands in by hand, while a game that sends one
//                            every 200 ms could otherwise write 430,000 rows a day that
//                            are kept until the account is erased (finding 11). Meals
//                            need no cap (one a meal time) and power none (one line a
//                            day).
//
// HOW THE PRICES WERE CHOSEN (game defaults for this increment):
//   - A MEAL is priced as one Basic Ration ("Vacuum-packed survival meal",
//     ration_basic_0, 10 CR): the one complete meal data/trade_goods.ron prices. That
//     file's own rule is 1 CR for about a minute of unskilled labour, so a crew meal is
//     about ten minutes of work.
//   - A KILOWATT-HOUR is 1.5 CR, by the same rule: the average US household price was
//     18.31 cents a kWh in July 2026 (U.S. Energy Information Administration, Electric
//     Power Monthly, Table 5.6.A, released 2026-09-24), and the federal minimum wage is
//     $7.25 an hour (U.S. Department of Labor, dol.gov, read 2026-10-04), 12.1 cents a
//     minute; 18.31 / 12.1 is 1.5 minutes of work. The same price both ways: power a
//     home returns to the ship is worth what power it draws costs.
//   - An ITEM given is worth its trade good's base_value, the number the vendor's
//     prices are built from.
//
//   max_give_quantity
//               the most of one item one give may carry: one full stack of the item
//               that stacks highest in data/items.csv (200, on 2026-10-04).
//   recent_entries
//               how many of a player's latest lines the ledger shows them.
//   power_report_min_interval_s
//               real seconds a game waits between power reports; the relay refuses one
//               sooner than this (the game sends one a minute).
//   power_report_window_s
//               the longest stretch, in real seconds, one power report may cover (at the
//               shared world's clock speed), so a broken or altered game cannot write a
//               year of power in one message.
//   home_service_watts
//               the most power one home can draw from the ship, or send back to it, at
//               any moment: no report is counted as more than this over the time it
//               covers. A GAME CHOICE, sized like a large house's electrical service:
//               200 amperes at 240 volts, 48 kW. (Until the review of 2026-10-04 the cap
//               was the reactor's whole 35 MW, which let one report a minute claim about
//               63,000 CR; finding 6.) The family home's life support averages about 2.6
//               kW (data/ship_power.ron), so an honest home sits far below it. The power
//               a game reports is still taken on its word until the server meters homes
//               itself: this only bounds how far a broken or altered game can move a
//               ledger.
//   totals_min_other_players
//               an admin sees the fleet's totals only when at least this many players
//               other than themselves have a ledger. With one other player, total minus
//               the admin's own lines IS that player's ledger, and asking again each
//               second shows each meal and gift as it happens (finding 9). Three keeps
//               any one person's lines inside a sum of at least three; a watchful admin
//               can still guess at who did what from who was online, which the admin
//               panel says.
//   gives_replayed
//               how many of a player's newest gives from one home the relay hands back
//               when that home's game asks (engine/fleet.rs settles again any its loaded
//               save does not list: the game closed before it saved, or a snapshot from
//               before the give was put back). A home's snapshots reach back at most a
//               few hours, so 200 gives covers far more than a save can miss.
(
    kinds: [
        (id: "meal", direction: Used, label: "Meal from the ship's stores", unit: "meal", price: OfGood("ration_basic_0"), per_day: false),
        (id: "item", direction: Contributed, label: "Given to the fleet", unit: "", price: OfItem, per_day: false, max_lines_per_day: Some(500)),
        (id: "item_creative", direction: Contributed, label: "Given in Creative mode (not counted)", unit: "", price: Fixed(0.0), per_day: false, max_lines_per_day: Some(500)),
        (id: "power_drawn", direction: Used, label: "Power from the ship's reactor", unit: "kWh", price: Fixed(1.5), per_day: true),
        (id: "power_returned", direction: Contributed, label: "Power returned to the ship", unit: "kWh", price: Fixed(1.5), per_day: true),
    ],
    max_give_quantity: 200,
    recent_entries: 20,
    power_report_min_interval_s: 30.0,
    power_report_window_s: 120.0,
    home_service_watts: 48000.0,
    totals_min_other_players: 3,
    gives_replayed: 200,
)
